    {
      "q": "How much federal contract money goes to Tennessee?",
      "a": "Tennessee received $158M in federal contract obligations in FY2027 to date. The state recorded 432 awards with an average award size of $365K, and obligations fell 98.7% year over year. Prior full-year totals were $11.4B in FY22, $11.2B in FY23, $10.8B in FY24, $11B in FY25, and $12.3B in FY26."
    },
    {
      "q": "Which agencies award the most contracts in Tennessee?",
      "a": "The Department of Veterans Affairs awards the most contracts in Tennessee in FY2027 to date with $144M. The Department of Justice follows with $14.8M, and the General Services Administration follows with $1.3M. Other agencies on the top-10 list include NASA at $1.2M and the Department of Labor at $961K."
